{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99455","id":2188878710,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Cd6N2","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99455","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99455.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99455.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99455","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99455/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99455/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99455/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e6daec9cf8b76a0cd8cc583c4ac0136d842b2a00","number":99455,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add indirect draw functionality to `MultiMesh`","user":{"login":"Bonkahe","id":11287274,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjg3Mjc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11287274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonkahe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonkahe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Currently has errors with the automated tests, not sure how to solve this, if anyone with experience could have a look and tell me what I'm missing, I'd be very grateful.\r\n\r\nImplements a new indirect mode to MultiMeshes, when allocating data a \"use_indirect\" Boolean can be set to true, initiating generation of a command buffer, this will be updated whenever a new mesh is added, and works with multiple surfaces, or theoretically non-indexed meshes, this hasn't been tested however.\r\n\r\nThe command buffer can be used to allow multimeshes, or any buffer alteration function, directly alter the number of instances drawn, in the example project is a C# implementation, as well as a GDScript test, which is much less robust.\r\n\r\nNEW example project:\r\nContains working frustum culling using compute shaders, and a simple grass model with implementation.\r\nZIP: [newindirectdrawmultimeshexample.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18328001/newindirectdrawmultimeshexample.zip)\r\nVideo: [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NPtDSJaN3cQ](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NPtDSJaN3cQ)\r\n\r\nNew project Gifs for eye candy purposes:\r\n![CommandBufferTests8](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a7b57cb9-e380-4a12-964a-a9271616fa3c)\r\n\r\nAlso some Examples of pausing the updating of the frustum culling, to show exactly what is being rendered by the gpu, with this method you can have an extreme amount of objects on screen with very good performance.\r\n![CommandBufferTests7](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/55ee8dd9-3208-4a01-bcdb-c448014619dc)\r\n![CommandBufferTests9](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/63427e3d-1616-45d3-b581-f7d2451027af)\r\n\r\n\r\nOLD:\r\nExample Project:\r\n[IndirectDrawMultimeshExample.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17824130/IndirectDrawMultimeshExample.zip)\r\n\r\nThe C# example in the project, 32k instances being enabled and disabled using a sine wave controlled through a compute shader with the command buffer bound to one of it's uniforms:\r\n![IndirectRenderingexample](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/819f760c-d8f9-477a-a3bf-f2a24295b4eb)\r\n\r\nThere's also a very ham-handed attempt at frustum culling in here which does not work, just an evening of me messing around with it.\r\n\r\nThings that may be able to be improved, the method by which I composite the data into the command buffer within the mesh_storage could be improved, I am inexperienced in handling vectors in c++ and as such ended up with a somewhat clumsy struct method of building the data. Every other attempt I had to just write to a single entry in the command buffer (for example to directly update the number of instances without touching anything else) resulted in errors, and even crashing my computer several times, so for now I figured I would go ahead and put out what I have, and see what you all think.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":10558797,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AoR1N","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/20","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/20","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repo